.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Kuhn (1934) modeled a flexible polymer as a random walk of n freely jointed segments of length b. freely_jointed_chain samples such conformations directly; averaging their squared end-to-end distance reproduces the exact result \langle R^2\rangle=nb^2 (~chemistrykit.polymer.systems.chain_statistics.IdealChain), and the end-to-end vector&#x27;s components become Gaussian with variance nb^2/3, as the central limit theorem predicts.">

